{
  "requirement": "Criteria obtain the agent selected by the domain's validation cache through\ntheir `ValidationContext`. The application supplies the configuration under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`. The SDK does not persist it.\nA cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.deterministic_procedures`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`.\n\n**Criteria obtain the domain cache's agent through their `ValidationContext`**\n- `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` builds the cache with `ValidationCache::with_agent(OpenAiConfig{endpoint,...})`. It then runs `validation::verify(&domain, Question(true))` twice.\n  - A local HTTP server receives four requests in total. They carry the configured model, the tool set and the `submit_result` schema.\n  - The criterion's answer is `true`. This shows the criterion reached the agent selected by the domain's cache.\n- `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat]` makes the same check for the Ollama backend, with the config attached through `with_agent`. It asserts the requests received and the final answer.\n- `agent/tests.rs#fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` and `providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supported_backend_settings_create_transports_without_sending_requests]` give further coverage of this obligation. The second one builds transports from the supported backend configs.\n\n**The SDK does not persist the configuration**\n- The OpenAI test serialises the stored `Record` after each `store_evidence` call. It asserts that the saved JSON contains none of `local-transport-key`, `local-test`, `backend` or `api_key`.\n- `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]` serialises the saved record after `refresh_evidence`. It asserts there is no `backend` key and that neither `development` nor `claude-sonnet` appears.\n- The same Bedrock test shows clones of the domain share the same configured agent, through `Arc::ptr_eq` and equality of the config.\n\n**Backend setup is deferred**\nThis comes from the cited `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`, and the tests cover it.\n- `configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors` asserts `agent.provider.get().is_none()` before and after a deterministic criterion.\n- The same test then checks that an awaited ask with a missing credential fails with `ValidationError::Agent` naming the credential variable.\n\n**A cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria**\n- `agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` uses `Memory::new`. Its cache is `Default::default()`, which has no agent. The test runs `validation::verify` and `store_evidence` on a deterministic `Review`. It asserts the output, the rationale and the recorded dependency.\n- `validation_tests.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` covers the other side. A criterion that asks an agent on an agentless cache returns `NoAgentConfigured` and stores nothing.\n\nTogether these cover the positive path, the no-agent path, non-persistence, laziness and sharing across clones. I found no plausible violation of the requirement that these tests would accept, so there are no gaps.",
  "references": "a7c327df3723dd097da425415d02491ba38f1398e61cad8e250b6b3934e6537e",
